---@meta
-- The Evil Islands rebuild's Lua API: the mission scripts' functions, the spells' cast value, methods and
-- hooks, the active effects' stats, the particle effects' hooks. For a Lua language server (VS Code's Lua
-- extension and others): docs/modding.md, "Lua in an editor".
-- Generated by ei-convert --lua-api from src/game/script/script_lua_api.inc
-- and src/engine/particles/particle_lua_api.inc. Do not edit.

---A map object: a unit, an item, a lever, ... A function that takes one takes nil for none.
---@class ei.Object

---A group of objects (a value shared as a table is: CopyGroup copies it): #group, group[i] from 1.
---@class ei.Group
---@field [integer] ei.Object?
---@operator len: integer

---A point or an object (where it stands).
---@alias ei.Position ei.Point|ei.Object

---A stats total's name (OnStats).
---@alias ei.StatName
---| "FireProtection" # added to the unit's protection from fire (the protection spells and antimagic: `Larger`)
---| "LightningProtection" # added to the unit's protection from lightning
---| "AcidProtection" # added to the unit's protection from acid
---| "Sight" # added to the sight range (eagle sight)
---| "DaySight" # added to the sight's percentage by day (infravision)
---| "NearSense" # added to the range sensed whatever the light (detect life)
---| "SightConspicuity" # added to how visible the unit is, which stays at least 0 (invisibility subtracts its value in percent)
---| "HearingConspicuity" # added to how loud the unit is, at least 0 (silence subtracts its value)
---| "NearConspicuity" # added to how near the unit is sensed, at least 0 (lichdom subtracts its value)
---| "SmellConspicuity" # added to how the unit smells (stench)
---| "Haste" # added to the action rate, which stays at least 1 (speed adds its value, slow subtracts its)
---| "Might" # hit points times (1 + `Might` x 0.005) / (1 + `Frailty` x 0.005), at least 1, and the unit's damage the same with 0.003 (strength)
---| "Frailty" # the divisor of `Might`'s formula (weak)
---| "Regeneration" # while above 0, the hit points regenerate that many times as fast (regeneration)
---| "Girth" # the figure grows by 0.4 a step: with `Size` 0, `Girth` steps wider (for the hero only in width), else `Size` + `Girth` steps on every axis (strength and weak 1 and -1)
---| "Size" # steps of the figure's size on every axis (enlarge and shrink 1 and -1)
---| "Stunned" # while above 0 the unit is stunned: no actions (stun; the teleport's arrival)
---| "NoCasting" # while above 0 the unit casts no spells, unless its natural weapon is spells only (feeblemind)
---| "Strength" # added to the strength (after the skill levels'): with it the hit points, the carried weight and the skills it leads (no game buff touches this one or those below)
---| "Dexterity" # added to the dexterity: with it the mana, the action rate and the skills it leads
---| "Intelligence" # added to the intelligence: with it the experience gained and the magic skills
---| "MaxHitPoints" # added to the hit point maximum, before `Might`'s scale
---| "MaxMana" # added to the mana maximum of a hero or a named unit (another unit's is its prototype's, unchanged)
---| "HitPointRegen" # added to the share of the maximum the hit points regenerate every 15 ticks while hurt (0.005: half a percent), before `Regeneration`'s factor
---| "ManaRegen" # added to the share of the maximum the mana regenerates every 15 ticks out of a fight
---| "PiercingProtection" # added to the unit's protection from piercing
---| "SlashingProtection" # added to the unit's protection from slashing
---| "CrushingProtection" # added to the unit's protection from crushing
---| "GeneralProtection" # added to the unit's protection from general damage
---| "Hearing" # added to the hearing range
---| "Smell" # added to the sense of smell
---| "Attack" # added to the attack of the unit's blows and shots (whole numbers count)
---| "Defence" # added to the defence against blows (whole numbers count; none against shots)
---| "Damage" # added to the damage of a weapon's or a natural attack's hit, before `Might`'s scale
---| "Speed" # added to the movement speed, which stays at least 0
---| "MeleeSkill" # added to the melee skill (the attack and defence with a blade, an axe, a club, ...)
---| "ArcherySkill" # added to the archery skill (bows and crossbows)
---| "ElementalSkill" # added to the elemental magic skill (fire, lightning, acid: what spells it may cast)
---| "SenseSkill" # added to the sense magic skill (illusion, divination)
---| "AstralSkill" # added to the astral magic skill (enchantment, healing, domination)
---| "Science" # added to the science (the Use and Steal skills)
---| "Taming" # added to the taming

---@class ei.Point
---@field x number
---@field y number
---@field z number

---@class ei.FindUnitsFilter
---@field enemies? boolean # only the caster's enemies (with no caster every unit is an enemy)
---@field friends? boolean # only the caster's friends
---@field alive? boolean # only living units
---@field area? boolean # only those area spells hit
---@field sight? boolean # only those in the line of sight the spell needs from at
---@field affect? boolean # only those the rune filters let the spell hit
---@field exclude? table<integer, boolean> # a set of ids to leave out: `{[GetObjectID(unit)] = true}`
---@field along? ei.Point # a direction: only those within 0.5 of the upright plane through at along it, as the game's walls hit
---@field unsorted? boolean # in the map's own order (the order the game's area spells hit in), not nearest first

---@class ei.DamageOptions
---@field area? boolean # a hit with no direction, as the walls' and clouds'
---@field noCredit? boolean # the caster is not the attacker
---@field split? number # shares the hit between n targets as the game's area spells do (n above 1: the amount and the hit's strength x 4 / n; they pass `cast.duration`)

---@class ei.ApplyOptions
---@field ticks? integer # how long it lasts (the cast's duration)
---@field power? number # its look's size (the cast's power)
---@field value? number # its value, `effect.value` in `OnStats` (the cast's damage)
---@field strength? number # its strength (the cast's radius)

---@class ei.MoveOptions
---@field check? boolean # only to a place the unit can stand on (true)

---@class ei.BoltOptions
---@field width? number # the bolt's width
---@field lifetime? integer # ticks it lasts (else as long as the cast)
---@field demon? boolean # the curse magic's look

---@class ei.MissileOptions
---@field to? ei.Object # the unit it flies at
---@field from? ei.Position # where it starts (the caster)
---@field effect? string # its particle effect (FireArrow)
---@field size? number # the effect's size (the cast's power)
---@field sound? string # the sound it makes in flight
---@field payload? any # given to OnHit

---@class ei.EffectOptions
---@field at? ei.Position # where it shows (the cast's point)
---@field attach? ei.Object # the unit it shows on
---@field size? number # its size (1)
---@field alpha? number # its opacity (1)
---@field param? number # its source's parameter (the fire blast's spread: the fireball passes its radius)
---@field velocity? ei.Point # it flies by so much a tick
---@field target? ei.Position # a flying one heads for this point
---@field unit? ei.Object # a flying one starts on the players' screens at this unit's hand (the fireball)
---@field direction? ei.Point # a wall effect's ([server] wall: Tendril, Link) extent from its middle to an end (the fire wall's)
---@field lifetime? integer # ticks it lasts (else as long as the cast)
---@field free? boolean # not the cast's: it lives its own life

---@class ei.SoundOptions
---@field volume? number # its volume
---@field hearing? number # how far it is heard
---@field velocity? ei.Point # it moves by so much a tick

---@class ei.SoundLoopOptions
---@field first? string # the sound played once before the loop
---@field volume? number # their volume
---@field hearing? number # how far they are heard
---@field velocity? ei.Point # they move by so much a tick
---@field lifetime? integer # ticks they last (else as long as the cast)

---@class ei.LightOptions
---@field color? number[] # {r, g, b} (the record's light_color)
---@field range? number # its range (the record's light_range)
---@field rise? number # it rises by so much a tick
---@field velocity? ei.Point # it moves by so much a tick
---@field lifetime? integer # ticks it lasts (else as long as the cast)

---@class ei.GroundOptions
---@field above? number # so much higher
---@field water? boolean # on the water's surface where there is water

---@class ei.VisionOptions
---@field lifetime? integer # ticks it lasts (else as long as the cast)

---@class ei.BlockOptions
---@field along? ei.Point # the wall's half: from `at - along` to `at + along`
---@field radius? number # a disc of that radius instead

---@class ei.Flight
---@field ticks integer # the ticks the flight takes
---@field distance number # its length along the ground
---@field speed number # its speed a second
---@field velocity ei.Point # its velocity a tick, for Effect's velocity

---A cast of a scripted spell: the same table at every hook of the cast, its fields brought up to date before each.
---@class ei.Cast
---@field id integer # the cast's number
---@field code string # the spell's code
---@field caster ei.Object? # the unit that cast it, or nil
---@field target ei.Object? # the unit it was cast at, or nil (also once it is gone)
---@field from ei.Point # where the cast started
---@field point ei.Point # the point it was cast at
---@field tick integer # ticks since the cast
---@field damage number # the spell's damage (runes included, as every number here)
---@field range number # its range
---@field radius number # its radius
---@field duration integer # its duration in ticks
---@field targetCount integer # its number of targets
---@field speed number # its speed
---@field mana number # its mana cost
---@field power number # the game's power curve of its damage, about 0.8 to 1.8
---@field areaPower number # the same curve of its area over the record's (the fireball's blast is the larger of the two)
---@field lightRise number # how fast the game's spell lights rise away: the record's `light_range / max(light_rise_divisor, 1)` a tick
---@field lightRange number # the record's `light_range`
---@field school string # its school's name
---@field silent boolean # an item's own periodic cast: the game's buffs end without their sound and its healing makes no sound or light on a unit at full health
---@field data table # a table of your own, kept with the cast and in saves: numbers, strings, booleans, units, tables
local Cast = {}

---the units within `radius` of `at`, nearest first (`filter`: FindUnitsFilter below)
---@param at ei.Position
---@param radius number
---@param filter? ei.FindUnitsFilter
---@return ei.Object[]
function Cast:FindUnits(at, radius, filter) end

---the spell's hits would hit the unit (its rune filters)
---@param unit ei.Object?
---@return boolean
function Cast:CanAffect(unit) end

---a spell's hit of `amount` of a damage type (`fire`, `lightning`, `acid`, `piercing`, `slashing`, `crushing`, `general`) on a unit (other objects are not hit): armour and protections count, the caster is the attacker unless `noCredit`. Gives the hit points lost
---@param unit ei.Object?
---@param amount number
---@param type string
---@param options? ei.DamageOptions
---@return number
function Cast:Damage(unit, amount, type, options) end

---heals as the healing spell does; gives the hit points gained
---@param unit ei.Object?
---@param amount number
---@return number
function Cast:Heal(unit, amount) end

---an active effect on the unit: `kind` a spell's code (`slow`, `stun`, `weak`, `prot_fire`, ...: that spell's effect and look) or `"own"` (this spell's, with its icon, doing what its `effect` says: nothing unless given). The values default to the cast's (duration, power, damage, radius)
---@param unit ei.Object?
---@param kind string
---@param options? ei.ApplyOptions
function Cast:Apply(unit, kind, options) end

---the unit's effects of that kind removed; how many
---@param unit ei.Object?
---@param kind string
---@return integer
function Cast:Remove(unit, kind) end

---whether the unit has an effect of that kind
---@param unit ei.Object?
---@param kind string
---@return boolean
function Cast:Has(unit, kind) end

---the unit moved to the point (at its own height) unless it cannot stand there; true when it moved. A push is a small move each tick
---@param unit ei.Object?
---@param to ei.Position
---@param options? ei.MoveOptions
---@return boolean
function Cast:Move(unit, to, options) end

---a lightning bolt; an end that is a unit follows it. Gives a handle
---@param from ei.Position
---@param to ei.Position
---@param options? ei.BoltOptions
---@return integer
function Cast:Bolt(from, to, options) end

---a spell missile flying at the unit `to` (at the game's missile speed) with the spell's light; `OnHit` runs when it lands. Gives a handle
---@param options ei.MissileOptions
---@return integer
function Cast:Missile(options) end

---a particle effect: one of yours (`Res\effects`, [Effects](#effects)) or a game's by its script name (`Sparks`, `LightningBlast`, `FireBlast`, `FireBall`, `Nuke`, `Healing`, ...). A `free` one (a flash that plays once) is not the cast's: it lives its own life, also after the cast ends. Gives a handle
---@param name string
---@param options? ei.EffectOptions
---@return integer
function Cast:Effect(name, options) end

---a sound played once (`magic\...\x.wav`), moving with `velocity`
---@param name string
---@param at ei.Position
---@param volume? number
---@param hearing? number
---@overload fun(name: string, at: ei.Position, options: ei.SoundOptions)
function Cast:Sound(name, at, volume, hearing) end

---sounds that go on while the cast holds them: `first` once, then `loop` (a name, or a list played in random order) over and over, as the fireball's flight and the walls sound. Gives a handle
---@param at ei.Position
---@param loop string|string[]
---@param options? ei.SoundLoopOptions
---@return integer
function Cast:SoundLoop(at, loop, options) end

---a point light, by default in the record's `light_color` and `light_range`, rising by `rise` a tick or moving by `velocity`. Gives a handle
---@param at ei.Position
---@param options? ei.LightOptions
---@return integer
function Cast:Light(at, options) end

---the cast's bolt, missile, effect or light of that handle moves by so much a tick from now on (a light sent up as it fades); false when it is gone
---@param handle integer
---@param velocity ei.Point
---@return boolean
function Cast:SetVelocity(handle, velocity) end

---an input of the cast's effect of that handle (one of yours, `Res\effects`) set for every player: a number, a flag, a choice by its name or a vector; false when it is gone or has no such input
---@param handle integer
---@param input string
---@param value number|boolean|string|ei.Point
---@return boolean
function Cast:SetInput(handle, input, value) end

---an event input of the cast's effect of that handle fired for every player; false when it is gone or has no such event
---@param handle integer
---@param event string
---@return boolean
function Cast:Fire(handle, event) end

---the point a unit's spells start from (its eye), where the game's lightning puts its light
---@param unit ei.Object?
---@return ei.Point
function Cast:Eye(unit) end

---the point where a hit on the unit shows, as the game's missiles splash: the ground below it plus its height as it stands (lower crawling, lying or dead, so ask after the damage); another object's position
---@param unit ei.Object?
---@return ei.Point
function Cast:HitPoint(unit) end

---whether it is a unit (false for nil, a unit that is gone, or another object)
---@param object ei.Object?
---@return boolean
function Cast:IsUnit(object) end

---the point on the ground at that place, `above` higher; `water`: on the water's surface where there is water, as the game's area spells aim
---@param at ei.Position
---@param options? ei.GroundOptions
---@return ei.Point
function Cast:Ground(at, options) end

---a flight along the ground at `speed` a second (default the spell's; 5 without one): the ticks it takes and the velocity a tick for `Effect`'s `velocity`
---@param from ei.Position
---@param to ei.Position
---@param speed? number
---@return ei.Flight
function Cast:Flight(from, to, speed) end

---the cast's bolt, missile, effect, light or sound loop of that handle goes now (a missile's `OnHit` never runs); false when it is gone or the handle is nil
---@param handle? integer
---@return boolean
function Cast:Release(handle) end

---the caster (a unit; nothing otherwise) makes a noise there that hostile units near it hear and come looking for the caster, as the fireball's blast does (`delay` the AI's call delay, 26 unless given)
---@param at ei.Position
---@param loudness number
---@param delay? integer
function Cast:Noise(at, loudness, delay) end

---the vector `{x, y, 0}` `length` long square to the ground line from `from` to `to` (to its left; along x when the two stand on one spot), as the game's walls stand across the line from their caster to their point: the wall's half from its middle to an end
---@param from ei.Position
---@param to ei.Position
---@param length number
---@return ei.Point
function Cast:Across(from, to, length) end

---the point where the object is (its own position, not the ground below it), where the teleport's departure shows
---@param object ei.Object?
---@return ei.Point
function Cast:Position(object) end

---whether the unit is dead, as the game's spells test it; false for nil or another object
---@param unit ei.Object?
---@return boolean
function Cast:IsDead(unit) end

---whether the unit's hit points as the players see them are not its maximum (the healing's test); false for nil or another object
---@param unit ei.Object?
---@return boolean
function Cast:IsHurt(unit) end

---the unit says an ack to its player, by acks.db's names (`"cant_teleport"`, `"link_ended"`, ...), as the teleport's caster says it cannot go
---@param unit ei.Object?
---@param ack string
function Cast:Shout(unit, ack) end

---the caster's player sees the unit this tick, as clairvoyance shows the units around its point (call it every tick)
---@param unit ei.Object?
function Cast:Reveal(unit) end

---the units within radius of the position wake, as fireworks and clairvoyance wake those around them
---@param at ei.Position
---@param radius number
function Cast:Wake(at, radius) end

---the unit's AI notices the position at `level` when that is above what it noticed last: fireworks frighten with 300 falling to 50 over their duration
---@param unit ei.Object?
---@param at ei.Position
---@param level integer
function Cast:Notice(unit, at, level) end

---the fog of war shows what the unit `seer` sees with the unit `observer`'s senses, as vision fog shows its caster what its target sees. Gives a handle
---@param seer ei.Object?
---@param observer ei.Object?
---@param options? ei.VisionOptions
---@return integer
function Cast:Vision(seer, observer, options) end

---the ground under a wall from `at - along` to `at + along`, or a disc of `radius` around `at`, counts as blocked for the units' paths (they go round it, as round the game's walls and clouds) until `Unblock` or the cast's end; one at a time (a second `Block` replaces the first). `Block` also works in `OnResume`
---@param at ei.Position
---@param options ei.BlockOptions
function Cast:Block(at, options) end

---the ground `Block` blocked is free again; whether there was one
---@return boolean
function Cast:Unblock() end

---a timer: the spell file's function of that name runs that many ticks later: `spell.Name(cast, payload)`
---@param ticks number
---@param name string
---@param payload? any
function Cast:After(ticks, name, payload) end

---the cast ends after this hook (its bolts, effects and lights go with it)
function Cast:Finish() end

---OnStats' totals.
---@class ei.Stats
local Stats = {}

---the total plus `x`
---@param name ei.StatName
---@param x number
function Stats:Add(name, x) end

---the total minus `x`
---@param name ei.StatName
---@param x number
function Stats:Subtract(name, x) end

---the larger of the total and `x`: how a protection and antimagic's take the larger of the two
---@param name ei.StatName
---@param x number
function Stats:Larger(name, x) end

---the total times `x`
---@param name ei.StatName
---@param x number
function Stats:Multiply(name, x) end

---OnStats' effect: one kind of active effect on a unit.
---@class ei.Effect
---@field kind string # its spell's code (lower case)
---@field value number # the strongest value of its kind's effects on the unit (from 0; the spell's damage unless `cast:Apply` gave one)

---The one-shot hooks' effect (OnEffectApplied, OnEffectEnded, OnEffectTick): one active effect on a unit; its methods work only in its hook.
---@class ei.ActiveEffect
---@field kind string # its spell's code (lower case)
---@field value number # its value (the spell's damage unless `cast:Apply` gave one)
---@field ticks integer # the ticks it has left
---@field power number # its look's size (its cast's power)
local ActiveEffect = {}

---a hit of `amount` of a damage type on the unit, as `cast:Damage`'s without a caster (no one has the credit; `noCredit` is not read). Gives the hit points lost
---@param amount number
---@param type string
---@param options? ei.DamageOptions
---@return number
function ActiveEffect:Damage(amount, type, options) end

---heals the unit as `cast:Heal` does; gives the hit points gained
---@param amount number
---@return number
function ActiveEffect:Heal(amount) end

---the effect taken off the unit now (its `OnEffectEnded` follows, `"removed"`); whether it was still on
---@return boolean
function ActiveEffect:Remove() end

---A spell file's table (Res\spells\<file>.lua returns it; annotate it `---@type ei.Spell`): the hooks, each optional, and the timers cast:After names.
---@class ei.Spell
---@field OnCast? fun(cast: ei.Cast) # once, when the cast starts
---@field OnTick? fun(cast: ei.Cast) # every tick after `OnCast` (a file with it keeps its casts going until `cast:Finish()` or the limit)
---@field OnHit? fun(cast: ei.Cast, target: ei.Object?, payload: any, point: ei.Point) # a missile of the cast landed: `target` nil when the unit is gone, `payload` what `cast:Missile` was given, `point` where it ended
---@field OnEnd? fun(cast: ei.Cast, reason: "finished"|"idle"|"limit"|"error") # once, at the end of the cast: `reason` `"finished"`, `"idle"`, `"limit"` or `"error"`
---@field OnResume? fun(cast: ei.Cast, old: {state: "missile"|"lasting", ticks: integer, visual?: integer, sound?: integer, light?: integer, direction?: ei.Point}) # a save made before a game's spell moved onto this file held a cast of it in flight (`old.state` `"missile"`) or lingering (`"lasting"`), `old.ticks` left on the game's own count: the cast's objects are already its own (a missile still lands in `OnHit`, with a nil payload; `old.visual`, `old.sound` and `old.light` are their handles, for `cast:Release` later; `old.direction` the direction of its wall or bolt); set its timers and data here (the world methods are off in this hook, but `cast:Block`). Without it such a cast ends at once
---@field OnStats? fun(effect: ei.Effect, stats: ei.Stats) # the effect's kind on a unit works out its stats ([Active effects](#active-effects)); the world's functions are off in it
---@field OnEffectApplied? fun(effect: ei.ActiveEffect, unit: ei.Object?) # an effect of the spell's kind came on a unit ([Active effects](#active-effects)), run at the end of that tick
---@field OnEffectEnded? fun(effect: ei.ActiveEffect, unit: ei.Object?, reason: "expired"|"removed"|"renewed"|"died") # an effect of the spell's kind left a unit: `reason` `"expired"` (its ticks ran out), `"removed"` (`cast:Remove`, `effect:Remove`), `"renewed"` (a new one of the kind and strength replaced it) or `"died"` (the unit died)
---@field OnEffectTick? fun(effect: ei.ActiveEffect, unit: ei.Object?) # every tick an effect of the spell's kind lasts on a unit, after its count down (`effect.ticks` left, above 0)
---@field [string] fun(cast: ei.Cast, payload: any)

---A particle effect's source in its script's hooks: a table of the script's own, kept from hook to hook (`e.ring = 0`), with these methods; they work only in its own hook.
---@class ei.EffectSource
local EffectSource = {}

---sets an input: a float, bool or enum (by its value's name or its index), a vector, a list's points; false when the effect has no such input of that type
---@param input string
---@param value number|boolean|string
---@overload fun(input: string, x: number, y: number, z: number)
---@overload fun(input: string, points: ei.Point[])
---@return boolean
function EffectSource:set(input, value) end

---fires an event input (its reactions run in this tick's step when fired before it, else at the next); false when the effect has none of that name
---@param event string
---@return boolean
function EffectSource:fire(event) end

---a value of the effect: an input (a vector's x, y, z; an enum's value name; a list's count), a var (its numbers), `stage` (its name, nil before the first) or a source value as the expressions name it (`age`, `size`, `origin` (x, y, z), `count`, `carrier_radius`, ...)
---@param name string
---@return any
function EffectSource:get(name) end

---a random number in [lo, hi) (without them in [0, 1)) from the particles' own generator
---@param lo? number
---@param hi? number
---@return number
function EffectSource:random(lo, hi) end

---a random whole number from 0 to n - 1, the same way
---@param n integer
---@return integer
function EffectSource:pick(n) end

---the ground's height at the point
---@param x number
---@param y number
---@return number
function EffectSource:ground(x, y) end

---starts another effect, free, at the source's origin or at the point
---@param name string
---@param x? number
---@param y? number
---@param z? number
function EffectSource:effect(name, x, y, z) end

---A particle in its effect's on_spawn and on_update; its methods work only in that call.
---@class ei.Particle
local Particle = {}

---`position`, `velocity` (x, y, z), `size`, `alpha` (0..255), `frame`, `color` (r, g, b, 0..255 each), `age`, `life` (ticks left), `kind` (its kind's name) or a var of its kind (its numbers)
---@param name string
---@return any
function Particle:get(name) end

---sets `position` or `velocity` (x, y, z), `size`, `alpha`, `frame`, `color` (r, g, b), `life` or a var of its kind
---@param name string
---@param ... number
function Particle:set(name, ...) end

---the particle dies at this update (its `on_death` runs); in `on_spawn` it is not kept
function Particle:kill() end

---A particle effect's script's table (Res\effects\<file>.lua returns it, the effect's `script` names it; annotate it `---@type ei.EffectScript`): the hooks, each optional.
---@class ei.EffectScript
---@field on_start? fun(e: ei.EffectSource) # once, at the effect's first tick, before its data starts (its vars, its first stage): inputs set here are what the start reads
---@field on_tick? fun(e: ei.EffectSource, age: integer) # every tick (the first too, after `on_start`), before the data's step; `age` counts the ticks from 0
---@field on_event? fun(e: ei.EffectSource, name: string, count: integer) # after `on_tick`, for each event input fired since the last tick (`count`: how many times), `"stop"` when the game stopped the emission and `"spawn"` when the game's effect object put the effect into the world (count 1); `"end"` once, after the step in which the effect ended
---@field on_spawn? fun(e: ei.EffectSource, p: ei.Particle, index: integer) # each particle the data made, once it is made (`index`: its number in this tick's emission); within the particle budget
---@field on_update? fun(e: ei.EffectSource, p: ei.Particle) # opt-in: each live particle, after the data moved it; within the particle budget, past it the data alone moves it

-- The mission scripts' functions (also in the spells' hooks).

-- ---- Script flow

---the script's globals, each set to its type's zero value: `{ name = "float" | "string" | "object" | "group" }` (0, `""`, nil, an empty group)
---@param declarations table<string, string>
function GlobalVars(declarations) end

---a definition: each call starts an instance with those arguments, which checks its rules in order every tick and runs the action of one that holds
---@param rules {condition?: fun(...): number|boolean, action?: fun(...)}[]
---@return fun(...)
function Script(rules) end

---waits that many ticks, then the function goes on (a function argument is called again on every tick)
---@param ticks number|fun(): number
function Sleep(ticks) end

---waits until the running instance has run that many ticks
---@param ticks number|fun(): number
function WaitSegment(ticks) end

---waits until the condition holds (pass a function: it is called again on every tick)
---@param condition number|fun(): number
function SleepUntil(condition) end

---waits while the unit's AI has an action under way
---@param unit ei.Object|fun(): ei.Object
function SleepUntilIdle(unit) end

---the running instance checks no more rules (not in the WorldScript)
function KillScript() end

---does nothing (as in the game)
function WaitEndAnimation() end

-- ---- Groups and loops

---an empty group
---@return ei.Group
function NewGroup() end

---a copy of the group (a group value is shared, as a table is; the game's assignment copied)
---@param group ei.Group
---@return ei.Group
function CopyGroup(group) end

---puts the object into the group (once)
---@param group ei.Group
---@param object ei.Object?
function AddObject(group, object) end

---takes the object out of the group
---@param group ei.Group
---@param object ei.Object?
function RemoveObject(group, object) end

---the number of objects in the group (also #group)
---@param group ei.Group
---@return number
function GroupSize(group) end

---1 when the object is in the group, else 0
---@param group ei.Group
---@param object ei.Object?
---@return number
function GroupHas(group, object) end

---a new group of the objects in either (the game's `GroupAdd`)
---@param a ei.Group
---@param b ei.Group
---@return ei.Group
function GroupUnion(a, b) end

---a new group of a's objects that are not in b (the game's `GroupSub`)
---@param a ei.Group
---@param b ei.Group
---@return ei.Group
function GroupDifference(a, b) end

---a new group of the objects in both (the game's `GroupCross`)
---@param a ei.Group
---@param b ei.Group
---@return ei.Group
function GroupIntersection(a, b) end

---a member at random (the game's generator); nil for an empty group (the game's `RandObj`)
---@param group ei.Group
---@return ei.Object?
function RandomObject(group) end

---calls the body for each member from the last to the first; a wait in the body ends it for that member. A counter global's name first: it holds each member in turn (the game's `For`)
---@param group ei.Group
---@param body fun(member: ei.Object)
---@overload fun(counter: string, group: ei.Group, body: fun(member: ei.Object))
function ForEach(group, body) end

---`ForEach`, the body only for the members the condition holds for (the game's `ForIf`)
---@param group ei.Group
---@param condition number|fun(member: ei.Object): number|boolean
---@param body fun(member: ei.Object)
---@overload fun(counter: string, group: ei.Group, condition: number|fun(member: ei.Object): number|boolean, body: fun(member: ei.Object))
function ForEachIf(group, condition, body) end

---1 when the condition holds for every member (from the first; it stops at one that fails), else 0
---@param group ei.Group
---@param condition number|fun(member: ei.Object): number|boolean
---@overload fun(counter: string, group: ei.Group, condition: number|fun(member: ei.Object): number|boolean)
---@return number
function Every(group, condition) end

---1 when the condition holds for a member (from the first; it stops there), else 0
---@param group ei.Group
---@param condition number|fun(member: ei.Object): number|boolean
---@overload fun(counter: string, group: ei.Group, condition: number|fun(member: ei.Object): number|boolean)
---@return number
function Any(group, condition) end

---the sum of the condition's values over the members
---@param group ei.Group
---@param condition number|fun(member: ei.Object): number|boolean
---@overload fun(counter: string, group: ei.Group, condition: number|fun(member: ei.Object): number|boolean)
---@return number
function Sum(group, condition) end

